        {"param": "k", "low": 2, "high": 4, "choices": null}
      ],
      "family": "unrolled_k",
      "budget_share": 0.28
    },
    {
      "why": "Unrolled datapath with registers every m stages; large m (6-8) minimises register count, but it still carries N adders, so area should exceed iterative. Small share to confirm dominance and to cover the unlikely case where its higher Fmax changes the picture. Replaces the fully pipelined family, which it dominates at small m.",
